:R-HSA-446388  a            owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0008150 ;
        rdfs:comment        "The PINCH-ILK-Parvin complexes function in transducing diverse signals from ECM to intracellular effectors. Interacting partners for components of these complexes have been identified, a number of which regulate and/or mediate its functions in cytoskeletal remodeling and cell spreading (reviewed in Wu, 2004)." ;
